cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Masterwork in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Masterwork: a production line for an agent's character"
abstract: >-
  Masterwork makes the piece; it does not score it. A model reads a corpus
  of craft tales and is asked, one axis at a time, what it will hold to —
  anchorless, in one sitting — then distils its own answers into the
  standing text it will read on every later request. Candidates are sealed
  with what is needed to produce them again. Measurement is handed to a
  separate benchmark rather than performed here, so a run the judge marked
  self-judged cannot reach a threshold, and a gate that could not measure
  holds instead of passing.
type: software
authors:
